For UI/UX design of an interactive legal-AI benchmarking website, thoughts on Vercel v0, Google Stitch, Magic Patterns, Figma Make, or something else?

When released, the next iteration of OverfittingDicta(dot)com will:
- Provide transparent, interactive benchmark results, with PostgreSQL-backed evidence and justifications for individual scoring determinations;
- Rely on an updated grading pipeline incorporating Legal Parse v2 to better evaluate complex, nuanced, and multimodal outputs from Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, and other models;
- Operate independently of Harvey, Legora, and other commercial legal-AI platforms;
- Evaluate independent and open-source solutions on equal footing with commercial offerings;
- Eventually introduce new benchmarks based on real-world data (rather than synthetic AI-generated tasks), alongside grading methodologies that incorporate behavioral analysis.

I'm using coding agents for implementation, so I'm primarily interested in tools for UI/UX design.
